Cumbria Resilience Forum - Fenella - SITREP 6
Time of report: 15/01/2026 0800

1. SITUATION
Incident status: Active response
Wind gusts up to 70 mph on exposed routes.

2. SITES AND ROUTES
- A591 Dunmail Raise: remains closed (flooding)
- Queen Elizabeth School, Kirkby Lonsdale: open to pupils
- Riverside Community Centre: operating as a rest centre (run by Cumberland Council)
- A66 Keswick to Penrith: OPEN
- Glenridding Village Hall: open as rest centre (run by Westmorland and Furness Council)
- West Coast Main Line (Carlisle to Lancaster): no trains running
- Fellside: evacuated (run by Fellside Care)
- Pooley Bridge crossing: closed to all traffic
- Keswick School: open as rest centre (run by Cumberland Council)
- M6 Junctoin 40: now open, lane restrictions in place (run by NH)
- Cockermouth School: operating as a rest centre (run by Cumberland Council EP team)
- Northside Bridge: closed as a precaution

3. AGENCIES RESPONDING
Westmorland and Furness Council, Cumbria Police, NH, Cumberland Council

4. NEXT MEETING
SCG at 1600. Dial-in details as previously circulated.

